Photorealistic vintage 1968 recording studio progress bar channel, viewed perfectly straight-on, centered, spanning 90 percent of image width and about one quarter of its height, isolated on a pure flat black background (#000000). Shape: long horizontal rectangular casing. Frame: hand-rubbed dark mahogany timber casing bordered by an antique brushed brass bezel with brass corner screws. Inside: a recessed channel of dark acoustic cloth. Running the full length inside the channel, a musical staff of exactly five thin, perfectly straight, evenly spaced, parallel horizontal lines made of fine glowing golden-amber vacuum tube filaments. At the far left end of the five-line staff, exactly one ornate treble clef illuminated in glowing warm golden-orange filament light. Absolutely nothing else on the staff: no notes, no bar lines, no numbers, no text. Clean studio product photography, crisp focus, centered. Single object only, no watermark.
